  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="parampara-heading">
    <h2 id="parampara-heading">What is the Khyapa Parampara</h2>
    <p>
      The Khyapa Parampara is a devotional and tantric lineage rooted in
      Tarapith, in Bengal. Its name comes from the Khepa (also written Khyapa)
      &mdash; the &ldquo;divinely mad&rdquo; &mdash; for whom the Divine is not
      an idea to be studied but the only reality to be lived. What looks like
      madness to the world is, inside the tradition, the highest sanity: a life
      given wholly to Ma Kali, Ma Tara and Bhairav Baba.
    </p>
    <p>
      This archive follows that current through three figures: Param Guru Bama
      Khyapa; his youngest disciple, Gurubaba Shyama Khyapa; and his Shishya who
      speaks of them today, Shri Praveen Radhakrishnan (my Guru ❤️).
    </p>
  </section>

