    <div>
      <h2 id="bama-heading">Param Guru Bama Khyapa &mdash; the Living Bhairava</h2>
      <p>
        Param Guru Bama Khyapa, also called Bamdev, is the Guru of Gurubaba
        Shyama Khyapa. Tarapith remembers him as the Living Bhairava and as the
        son of Ma Tara: when Shiva drank the poison churned from the ocean, Tara
        took him to her lap to soothe him, and from that moment of the
        Mother&rsquo;s tenderness the form of Bama Khyapa arose.
      </p>
      <p>
        He was born into a poor Brahmin family and had little gift for
        scripture. What he had was the Name. He could not recite the Vedas, but
        when &ldquo;Ma Tara&rdquo; rose in him he would pass into samadhi. He
        made the cremation ground his home, sat with the dogs as his
        companions, and showed that the Divine is not reached through learning,
        procedure, or purity &mdash; but through the Name and through grace.
      </p>
      <a class="about-link" href="/articles/living-bhairava-bama-khepa-guru-parampara/">Read the full account &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>

