    <div>
      <h2 id="shyama-heading">Gurubaba Shyama Khyapa &mdash; the hidden master</h2>
      <p>
        Gurubaba Shyama Khyapa is the youngest disciple of Param Guru Bama
        Khyapa, and is known in this lineage as the Chathurthapurush, the fourth
        realized master. For most of his life he was a gupta sadhak &mdash; a hidden
        practitioner &mdash; bound by his Guru&rsquo;s command not to be known.
        His name has only recently come into the open.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before the path, his life was one of considerable wealth: a law and
        audit practice, a family, cars, a bungalow. A visit to Pashupatinath
        changed it. He heard an inner command to leave, handed the business to
        his partner, and walked out. He became a wandering monk and settled at
        the cremation ground of Tarapith, meditating by burning pyres and on the
        ash mound of Ugratara.
      </p>
      <a class="about-link" href="/articles/the-chathurthapurush-and-gupta-sadhak-shyamakhyapa/">Read his full story &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>

